@display("Features and context")
context: section {
  | A feature is a `section`: its intent in `|` text, then what it leaves out and its
  | requirements as children. Around the requirements stands what helps build them without
  | being required behaviour: the domain's words, hints for implementers and the
  | flags that let a reader find what cuts across features.

  feature_section: term {{
    `name: section { … }` holding a feature: its `|` text says the intent, an
    `outOfScope` says what's left out, and its rules, [lifecycles](#language.specifications.lifecycles.lifecycle) and qualities follow.
    Sections nest and are referenced by path, as `refund_window.late_rejected`.
  }}

  out_of_scope: term {{
    `name: outOfScope {{ … }}`, something a reader could reasonably expect the feature to
    cover that's deliberately left out.
  }}

  cross_cutting_section: term {{
    A section flagged `<security>`, `<privacy>` or `<operations>`. It holds requirements
    like any other, and the flag lets reviews and deciders find it and load it on its own.
  }}

  term_kind: term {{
    `name: term {{ … }}`, a word of the domain defined once, where its domain is. Its
    name read as words is the phrase it defines, so `capture_date` defines "capture
    date", and `aliases = […]` lists the synonyms it rules out. Prose links to it as
    `[capture date](#capture_date)`, a checked reference.
  }}

  guidance_kind: term {{
    `guidance(targets) {{ … }}`, hints for whoever builds its targets, such as an internal
    API to use or a convention to follow.
  }}

  passage: term {{
    A named span of wording, `<span name="window_wording">…</span>`, that [coverage](#language.specifications.traceability.coverage) can
    point at when the wording itself must be covered.
  }}

  out_of_scope_not_built: rule(out_of_scope, by = product.actors.implementer) {
    mustNot {{ build what a feature puts [out of scope](#language.specifications.context.out_of_scope) }}
  }

  out_of_scope_shown: rule(out_of_scope, by = product.system.docs_generator) {
    must {{ show an `outOfScope` and a `guidance` as callouts labelled "[Out of scope](#language.specifications.context.out_of_scope)" and "Guidance", with their text }}
  }

  flags_on_sections: rule(cross_cutting_section, by = product.system.linter) {
    should {{ report [flag placement](#language.schemas.flags.diagnostics.flag_misplaced) at `<security>`, `<privacy>` or `<operations>` on anything but a section }}
  }

  terms_linked: rule(term_kind, by = product.system.prose_linter) {
    should {{ report [unlinked term](#language.specifications.quality_checks.diagnostics.unlinked_term) where prose outside the term uses its phrase without linking it, and [ruled-out synonym](#language.specifications.quality_checks.diagnostics.ruled_out_synonym) where it uses one of its [aliases](#language.data.values.alias) }}
    then {{ a fix offered with it links the phrase, or replaces the [alias](#language.data.values.alias) with the linked term }}
  }

  one_sense: rule(term_kind, by = product.system.prose_linter) {
    should {{ report [two senses](#language.specifications.quality_checks.diagnostics.two_senses) at each of two terms that define one phrase, by name or by [alias](#language.data.values.alias) }}
  }

  term_shown: rule(term_kind, by = product.system.docs_generator) {
    must {{ show a term as an entry of a definition list, its name and its text }}
  }

  guidance_not_required: rule(guidance_kind, by = product.system.linter) {
    mustNot {{ count guidance as a requirement or as covered }}
  }

  stale_guidance: rule(guidance_kind, by = product.system.linter) {
    if {{ guidance names a symbol of the code that no longer exists }}
    should {{ report the name as a [dead link](#language.specifications.quality_checks.diagnostics.dead_link) }}
  }

  values_in_surface: rule(feature_section, by = product.actors.author) {
    should {{ keep the values code depends on in the surface or the data, as a type, a [value binding](#language.data.configuration.value_binding) or a quality, rather than in a rule's text }}
    example {{ a rule mentions "30 days", and the value an implementation reads comes from a type }}
  }

  out_of_scope_hint: rule(feature_section, by = product.system.linter) {
    if {{ a section holds requirements and no `outOfScope` }}
    may {{ give a hint that the section says nothing of what it leaves out }}
  }
}
